  "summary": "This study compares five freestanding Ti3C2-based film electrodes: pristine Ti3C2 and four N-doped variants prepared with 0.5, 1.5, 2.0, or 3.0 g urea during solvothermal treatment. The starting single/few-layer Ti3C2 nanosheets were made by LiF/HCl etching of Ti3AlC2 followed by ultrasonication delamination. The headline 2.0 N-Ti3C2 electrode delivered 1609.5 F g-1 and 2898.5 F cm-3 at 2 mV s-1 in 3 M H2SO4. Film thickness, active-material loading, BET surface area, pore metrics, and numerical capacitances for 3.0 N-Ti3C2 were not reported."
